    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task required `GET /api/owners/{id}` to return `selfLink` = `/api/owners/` + the owner's id. This codebase exposes derived owner fields via a consistent pattern: a read-only getter on the `Owner` entity plus a `readOnly` property in the OpenAPI schema, which MapStruct maps into the generated `OwnerDto` automatically. I followed that same idiom:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `selfLink` `readOnly` string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the other derived fields like `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, etc.), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `selfLink` field and setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added `getSelfLink()`:\n   ```java\n   public String getSelfLink() {\n       return \"/api/owners/\" + this.getId();\n   }\n   ```\n\nNo mapper or controller changes were needed \u2014 MapStruct picks up the getter/property by name.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsSelfLink` passes, and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the acceptance test is the only test class in the project).",
